<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Campaign</p><h1 class="enc-title">Brusilov Offensive</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1916">1916</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Brusilov Offensive was a major Russian attack on the Eastern Front from June to September 1916 during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>, led by General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexei-brusilov">Alexei Brusilov</a> along a front of about 480 kilometres. It inflicted enormous losses on the Austro-Hungarian army, estimated at 600,000 to one million men. The offensive left the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Austro-Hungarian Empire</a> dependent on German military support.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/brusilov-offensive.jpg" alt="Brusilov Offensive" width="320" height="248" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Department of Military Art and Engineering, at the U.S. Military Academy (West Point) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:EasternFront1916b.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
